WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.199
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.499 --> 00:00:08.503
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.803 --> 00:00:14.949
Unit fifteen: Heritage and Identity. In this unit, you will discuss culture, heritage and identity.

4
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.265
cultural heritage.

5
00:00:17.965 --> 00:00:23.006
cultural heritage means traditions, buildings and art passed down through generations.

6
00:00:23.306 --> 00:00:26.025
Angkor is part of Cambodia's cultural heritage.

7
00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:29.296
Your turn. Say: cultural heritage.

8
00:00:31.996 --> 00:00:33.334
cultural heritage.

9
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.270
identity.

10
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:39.606
identity means who a person or group is; what makes them different.

11
00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:42.649
Language is an important part of our identity.

12
00:00:43.349 --> 00:00:45.502
Your turn. Say: identity.

13
00:00:48.202 --> 00:00:49.284
identity.

14
00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.238
ancestry.

15
00:00:51.938 --> 00:00:55.122
ancestry means the people in your family who lived long ago.

16
00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:57.944
She traced her ancestry back to Battambang.

17
00:00:58.644 --> 00:01:00.936
Your turn. Say: ancestry.

18
00:01:03.636 --> 00:01:04.695
ancestry.

19
00:01:05.683 --> 00:01:06.731
tradition-bound.

20
00:01:07.431 --> 00:01:10.522
tradition-bound means strongly following old customs.

21
00:01:10.822 --> 00:01:12.961
The village is quite tradition-bound.

22
00:01:13.661 --> 00:01:16.650
Your turn. Say: tradition-bound.

23
00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.687
tradition-bound.

24
00:01:21.683 --> 00:01:22.557
folklore.

25
00:01:23.257 --> 00:01:26.499
folklore means traditional stories and beliefs of a community.

26
00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:28.926
Khmer folklore is full of clever rabbits.

27
00:01:29.626 --> 00:01:31.674
Your turn. Say: folklore.

28
00:01:34.374 --> 00:01:35.271
folklore.

29
00:01:36.283 --> 00:01:37.377
craftsmanship.

30
00:01:38.077 --> 00:01:40.982
craftsmanship means the skill of making things by hand.

31
00:01:41.282 --> 00:01:44.269
The craftsmanship of the silver bowls is amazing.

32
00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:47.668
Your turn. Say: craftsmanship.

33
00:01:50.368 --> 00:01:51.798
craftsmanship.

34
00:01:52.783 --> 00:01:53.831
silk weaving.

35
00:01:54.531 --> 00:01:58.434
silk weaving means making cloth from silk thread on a loom.

36
00:01:58.734 --> 00:02:01.373
Silk weaving is a traditional skill on Koh Dach.

37
00:02:02.073 --> 00:02:04.725
Your turn. Say: silk weaving.

38
00:02:07.425 --> 00:02:08.589
silk weaving.

39
00:02:09.583 --> 00:02:10.712
shadow puppetry.

40
00:02:11.412 --> 00:02:15.165
shadow puppetry means theatre using leather puppets in front of a light.

41
00:02:15.465 --> 00:02:19.171
Sbek Thom is a famous form of Khmer shadow puppetry.

42
00:02:19.871 --> 00:02:22.616
Your turn. Say: shadow puppetry.

43
00:02:25.316 --> 00:02:26.538
shadow puppetry.

44
00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.538
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:29.838 --> 00:02:32.987
Nita, you visited Koh Dach last weekend, didn't you?

46
00:02:34.283 --> 00:02:39.176
Yes! Walking through the village, I saw families doing silk weaving.

47
00:02:40.483 --> 00:02:42.448
Their craftsmanship is incredible.

48
00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:47.828
Having watched them for an hour, I understood how much patience it takes.

49
00:02:49.117 --> 00:02:50.872
Did you see any shadow puppetry?

50
00:02:52.183 --> 00:02:57.216
Yes. Performed by young artists, the show told stories from Khmer folklore.

51
00:02:58.517 --> 00:03:01.294
Grammar focus: Participle clauses.

52
00:03:01.594 --> 00:03:05.068
Participle clauses make writing shorter and more advanced.

53
00:03:05.368 --> 00:03:13.440
Use -ing for actions at the same time, having plus past participle for completed actions, and a past participle for a passive meaning.

54
00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:18.482
For example: Having finished the tour, we had lunch. Made by hand, the scarf is unique.

55
00:03:18.782 --> 00:03:25.367
The subject of the participle clause must be the same as the main clause: 'Walking home, I saw ...', not 'Walking home, the rain started'.

56
00:03:26.383 --> 00:03:29.187
Now read and listen. Keeping Traditions Alive.

57
00:03:29.487 --> 00:03:33.216
Many traditional skills in Cambodia were almost lost during the war.

58
00:03:34.517 --> 00:03:39.303
Rebuilt by dedicated artists, shadow puppetry is now performed again in Siem Reap.

59
00:03:40.617 --> 00:03:44.485
Having trained young people, master weavers are passing on the art of silk weaving.

60
00:03:45.783 --> 00:03:49.826
Folklore is also being recorded in books and videos for future generations.

61
00:03:51.117 --> 00:03:55.833
Protecting cultural heritage helps people understand their identity and ancestry.

62
00:03:57.117 --> 00:03:59.525
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:59.825 --> 00:04:02.730
Traditional stories and beliefs of a community are blank.

64
00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:06.510
A, folklore. B, ancestry. C, identity.

65
00:04:10.517 --> 00:04:12.296
The answer is A: folklore.

66
00:04:13.783 --> 00:04:16.108
blank the museum, we went to a café.

67
00:04:16.408 --> 00:04:19.910
A, Having visited. B, Visited. C, Have visited.

68
00:04:23.917 --> 00:04:25.800
The answer is A: Having visited.

69
00:04:27.317 --> 00:04:30.535
blank in the 12th century, the temple is very old.

70
00:04:30.835 --> 00:04:33.989
A, Building. B, Built. C, Having building.

71
00:04:37.983 --> 00:04:39.495
The answer is B: Built.

72
00:04:40.983 --> 00:04:43.296
The skill of making things by hand is blank.

73
00:04:43.596 --> 00:04:47.946
A, craftsmanship. B, tradition-bound. C, silk weaving.

74
00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:54.159
The answer is A: craftsmanship.

75
00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.822
According to the text, what is now performed again in Siem Reap?

76
00:04:59.122 --> 00:05:03.217
A, silk weaving. B, shadow puppetry. C, folklore.

77
00:05:07.217 --> 00:05:09.797
The answer is B: shadow puppetry.

78
00:05:11.283 --> 00:05:16.142
Now it's your turn to speak. Which tradition from your culture would you like to protect, and why?

79
00:05:21.442 --> 00:05:29.513
Having seen how few people learn it now, I'd like to protect traditional Khmer music, because it is part of our identity.

80
00:05:29.813 --> 00:05:31.290
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:32.283 --> 00:05:36.526
Great work today! You learned eight new words and participle clauses.

82
00:05:36.826 --> 00:05:40.512
Today's value is love of country. Love and take care of Cambodia.

83
00:05:40.812 --> 00:05:43.069
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

84
00:05:43.369 --> 00:05:45.859
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

